  <div class="about-story">
    <div class="about-story-intro"><p class="lead">Born in Mumbai, raised across Manchester and Umeå, and now at home in Uppsala, I grew up learning that identity can be expansive rather than fixed.</p><p>Moving between India, England, and Sweden made curiosity and adaptation part of everyday life. It also made community matter: wherever I landed, I wanted to understand the place, contribute to it, and help people feel included.</p><p>I completed upper-secondary school two years early, graduating at 17 after taking additional courses. That same appetite for challenge led me to Engineering Physics at Uppsala University and toward computational physics, embedded systems, software engineering, and research.</p></div>
    <ol class="origin-path" aria-label="Places that shaped me"><li><span>2007</span><strong>Mumbai</strong><p>Where the story began—during monsoon season, naturally.</p></li><li><span>2010–2016</span><strong>Manchester</strong><p>Where I learned English, British humour, and a suspicious tolerance for rain.</p></li><li><span>2016–2021</span><strong>Umeå</strong><p>Where northern winters taught resilience, layering, and the value of a good community.</p></li><li><span>2021–Now</span><strong>Uppsala</strong><p>Where studies, research, engineering, and student life became one very full timeline.</p></li></ol>
    <div class="about-life"><div><p class="kind">Beyond the formal CV</p><h2>Serious about the work.<br />Not solemn about life.</h2></div><div><p>I like sport, making admittedly questionable rap songs with friends, and watching far too many nerdy physics videos. I’m happiest around people who are both ambitious and able to laugh at themselves.</p><p>That combination shapes how I work: learn quickly, take responsibility, communicate clearly, and make enough room for other people to enjoy building alongside me.</p></div></div>
